Here's how to handle each scenario with modern MSTest (3.9+):

### 1. Windows-only tests — `[OSCondition]`
```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]
public void Registry_ReadsExpectedValue()
{
    var value = Registry.GetValue(@"HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\...", "Key", null);
    Assert.IsNotNull(value);
}
```

### 2. Skip in CI — `[CICondition]`
```csharp
[TestMethod]
[CICondition(ConditionMode.Exclude)]
public void GpuRendering_ProducesExpectedOutput()
{
    var result = GpuRenderer.Render(scene);
    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
}
```

### 3. Flaky external API — `[Retry]`
```csharp
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)]
[Timeout(10000)]
public async Task WeatherApi_ReturnsForecast(TestContext testContext)
{
    var forecast = await _weatherClient.GetForecastAsync(testContext.CancellationToken);
    Assert.IsNotNull(forecast);
}
```

Use `[Retry]` only for genuinely flaky external dependencies — not to mask race conditions.

### 4. Cleanup on failure — `[TestCleanup]`
```csharp
[TestClass]
public sealed class FileProcessingTests
{
    private string? _tempFile;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessFile_WritesExpectedContent()
    {
        File.WriteAllText(_tempFile!, "test data");
        var result = FileProcessor.Process(_tempFile!);
        Assert.AreEqual("processed", result);
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Runs even if the test fails or throws
        if (_tempFile is not null && File.Exists(_tempFile))
        {
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
        }
    }
}
```

### Combined example

You can stack all these attributes:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]
[CICondition(ConditionMode.Exclude)]
[Retry(2)]
[Timeout(15000)]
public async Task GpuWeatherWidget_RendersOnWindows(TestContext testContext)
{
    var data = await _weatherClient.GetAsync(testContext.CancellationToken);
    var image = GpuRenderer.Render(data);
    Assert.IsNotNull(image);
}
```

**Key points:**
- `[OSCondition]` and `[CICondition]` **skip** (not fail) when conditions aren't met (MSTest 3.10+)
- `[Retry(n)]` retries up to `n` times on failure (MSTest 3.9+)
- `[TestCleanup]` always runs — even on failure, timeout, or exception
- Pair `[Timeout]` with `TestContext.CancellationToken` for cooperative cancellation
